      <title>Trump Says FBI Reviewing Nvidia CEO Huang's Affair</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/videos/2026-11-10/daybreak-europe-11-10-2026-video</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">30e1fcdf66147286ba16b10d</guid>
      <pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 08:08:02 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Bloomberg Daybreak Europe is your essential morning viewing to stay ahead. Live from Berlin, we set the agenda for your day, catching you up with overnight markets news from the US and Asia. And we'll tell you what matters for investors in Europe, giving you insight before trading begins.

President Donald Trump said the FBI is looking into Nvidia Chief Executive Officer Jensen Huang’s extramarital relationship with a suspected Chinese spy, and offered his support to the embattled chip magnate a day after the affair was disclosed.

Anthropic is set to kick off the formal marketing of its blockbuster initial public offering as early as Tuesday after an apparent snafu over the filing documents added a dose of last-minute drama to a nervous market.

And global stocks were on track for their best two-day gain in more than three months as a resurgent tech rally and a further decline in oil prices boosted sentiment. (Source: Bloomberg)</description>
