      <description>If there were any doubts that America’s once-solid bonds to Israel are fraying, President Donald Trump laid them to rest on Nov. 3, the day Americans voted in congressional elections. The flow of some $4 billion annually in US military aid to Israel will stop, said Trump. He described the assistance as a “bad talking point” for his Republican Party, which in recent years has been more pro-Israel than the Democratic Party.</description>
